------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=500 daevas explanation demon 2
Text=The Persians gave the name Daevas to the major demonic forces, the Mongols knew them as the wicked Sholmos, and far to the east the Tibetans, who are as yet unknown to your people, fear them as the Sri. Some call them devils, but in every culture they embody evil incarnate - they certainly make things interesting on this drab mortal world!
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=500 daevas explanation demon part 2
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=500 daevas explanation demon part 2
Text=I'll be the first to admit that you shouldn't trust a Daeva, as their kind has tormented your kind throughout time. Each Daeva is unique and possesses a power over some evil aspect that they use to corrupt morals in different devious ways.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=You're a demon - are *you* a Daeva?
Go to node ID=1000 are you a daeva

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=You keep saying *so-called* Divine Ones. What are they?
